Fix the decreases-tuple comparison so weak real progress and equal sequence/datatype ranks cannot discard and reset a suffix. Calls, loops, overrides, termination-ordering expressions, and experimental modular global/callback bounds use compatible strict/weak component relations and TOP padding. Negative terminal numeric values remain supported. The corrected comparison is the default; a hidden `--legacy-decreases-order` switch retains the previous, unsound behavior for migration and comparison. See https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/264.
